        "date": "2026-11-08T21:04:32Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(setup): lay the part on a G17/G18/G19 plane from a picked face or two edges\n\nA setup row on the Setups page gets \"Lay on a plane\": pick one flat face,\nor two straight edges, in the viewport, choose G17 (XY), G18 (ZX) or G19\n(YZ), flip it, optionally set the face onto the plane's level, and Apply.\nThe app computes the rigid turn (pick::lay_on_plane: shortest arc for a\nface with the antiparallel case as a half turn about the plane's first\naxis; frame-to-frame for two edges, the first edge along X for G17/G18\nand Y for G19) and writes it as the setup's part alignment through\nAlignPartToSetup::lay_on_plane -> AlignPartToSetup::new (#326), one\nundoable command. The work offset is never touched.\n\nRefused by name: a curved or degenerate face, a vertex, a closed or\ncurved edge, parallel or coincident edges, a wrong pick count, a pick on\nthe stock or a fixture, a pick no longer in the model. The landing is\nproven (normal within 1e-9 rad of the axis) before anything is stored.\n\nThe 3-2-1's outward-normal and straight-edge readers take the frame as a\nparameter so both features share them; the 3-2-1 is unchanged.\n\nFixes #330\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
