      "message": "fix(setup): two-edge plane takes its outside from the face both edges bound\n\nReview on PR #346: the two-edge datum guessed its outward side from the\nparts' bounds centre - wrong on a concave part (an L-bracket step, a\npocket floor) and silently d1 x d2 on a plane through the centre. The\nside now comes from the one flat face both picked edges bound, read\nfrom that face's facet winding (the same outward_normal the face pick\nuses); the bbox-centre rule is gone. Edges that bound no common flat\nface (or lie on two bodies, or are skew) are refused by name: \"the two\nedges do not bound one face, so their outside is not defined - pick\nthe face instead\".\n\nReview notes folded in: the Setups row greys Apply out when the picks\ngive the alignment the setup already holds (AlignPartToSetup::check_lay,\nthe command's own check), and shows the side taken as outside before\nApply (pick::plane_side). New tests: plane_align_edges (concave step,\nplane through the centre, no common face, two bodies, degenerate face,\nupside-down tilted part's half turn) and a ui row test.\n\nRefs #330\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
